    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA very fine light-filled Victorian two storey over garden level home extending to approximately 217 sqm (2,335 sqft). Beautifully renovated and restored, it offers elegant, well-proportioned reception rooms, three double bedrooms upstairs and a fourth bedroom at garden level. Throughout, the house combines fine period detail with high-quality contemporary craftsmanship, including elegant interconnecting reception rooms, and a kitchen/breakfast room with double doors opening out to the rear garden.\n\nSuperbly positioned on an attractive terrace of just eight houses, the property is only moments from Leeson Street and Ranelagh Village, with their excellent shops, restaurants and cafés, and within comfortable walking distance of St Stephen's Green. Ranelagh Luas stop is about a five-minute walk away, providing easy access to the city centre, Sandyford and beyond. Families are also well served by some of South Dublin's most highly regarded junior and secondary schools, including Scoil Bhríde, Sandford Park, Gonzaga College, St Mary's College and Muckross Park.\n\nNumber 6 is a warm and welcoming home, ideal for entertaining. At hall level, elegant interconnecting living and dining rooms are rich in period detail, with high ceilings, fine marble fireplaces, attractive cornicing, a centre rose, panelled doors and large sash windows with working shutters. At garden level, a bright, well-equipped kitchen/breakfast room opens through double doors to the rear garden. To the front, the fourth bedroom includes an en-suite shower room and could also serve as an additional reception room. A practical utility room off the kitchen and excellent understairs storage complete the garden-level accommodation.\n\nUpstairs, there are three further generous double bedrooms, one with an en-suite, together with a family bathroom.\n\nOutside, the front and rear gardens are a standout feature. The railed and walled front garden has a gravelled centre, landscaped beds, hedging and a tiled pathway leading to the granite steps and hall door. A separate front entrance provides access to the garden level. To the rear, the private landscaped garden is a peaceful and stylish oasis with a pleasant south-easterly aspect, extending to approximately 20m/66ft. It includes a patio area, mature planting, hedging and a granite pathway leading to the rear. Valuable off-street parking is provided by a cobble-lock parking area with double gates accessed from a lane off Sallymount Avenue. There is also an outside water tap and a timber Barna shed offering excellent storage.\n\nThis stylish, warm and inviting family home combines immense charm and character with every conceivable amenity on its doorstep, making it ideal for those seeking a period home in Dublin 6."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall Floor Level - \n\n\nReception hall: - \nWith 12ft high ceilings, ceiling coving, centre rose, polished timber flooring and picture rail.\n\nDining Room: - \nTo the front, with high ceilings, ceiling coving, centre rose and picture rail. Restored magnificent marble fireplace with cast iron and tiled inset, copper hood, slate hearth and coal effect gas fire, sash window with window shutters. Bi-folding doors opening into the\n\nLiving Room: - \nTo the rear, with high ceilings, ceiling coving, centre rose and picture rail. Restored magnificent marble fireplace with cast iron and tiled inset, copper hood, slate hearth and coal effect gas fire, sash window with window shutters.A restored original staircase with polished mahogany handrail leads to the upper and lower floors\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nBedroom 1: - \nTo the rear, main bedroom, with high ceilings, painted cast iron fireplace, ceiling coving, centre rose and sash windows with window shutters.\n\nEnsuite: - \nWith wc, pedestal wash hand basin, shower with Mira Event electric shower, tiled walls and floors, heated towel rail and velux roof light.\n\nBedroom 2: - \nTo the front, laid out as an upstairs Sitting room/Lounge, with cast iron fireplace, polished timber flooring, ceiling coving and centre rose.\n\nBedroom 3: - \nTo the front, laid out as a home office/study, with cast iron fireplace, polished timber floors, sash window with window shutters.\n\nSecond Floor: - \n\n\nBathroom: - \nFully tiled bathroom with pedestal wash hand basin, wc, bath with telephone-style attachment, Electric shower (Mira) overhead, Heated towel rail, Window to the rear providing natural light.\n\nGarden Level: - \nSeparate entrance to the front, leading into\n\nEntrance and inner hallway: - \nwith tiled flooring. There is excellent storage throughout, including an under-stairs store/wine cellar, additional storage area, and two cloak cupboards.\n\nBedroom Four / Guest Room: - \nA spacious front facing guest bedroom with decorative ceiling coving and centre rose, sash window with plantation shutters, tiled flooring and feature antique wood-burning stove.\n\nEn Suite: - \nWith Pedestal wash hand basin, wc, corner shower unit, tiled flooring, fitted shelving and freestanding storage.\n\nGuest WC: - \nOff the inner hall, with pedestal wash hand basin, wc, wall panelling, tiled floor, mirror detailing.\n\nKitchen / Breakfast Room: - \nA bright and well-equipped space featuring, extensive range of fitted press and drawer units, Franke sink, Neff six-ring gas range cooker, integrated dishwasher, integrated Bosch fridge freezer, ceiling coving with recessed downlighting, tiled flooring, and double doors opening to the delightful rear garden.\n\nUtility Room: - \nWith Single drainer sink unit, Electrolux washing machine, ample storage presses, partially tiled walls and tiled floor, sash window to the rear.\n\n"
      },
      {
